    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">GST Structure</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The central Goods and Services Tax (GST) applies to the freight value. For standard freight services, the rate is 18%. However, if the transport is classified under the “special rate” category for inter‑state motor transport of goods, the reduced rate of 5% may be eligible.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>Operators must verify the classification against the latest GST notifications and file the appropriate GSTR‑1 and GSTR‑3B returns</span>
  </li>
</ul>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">GST Compliance</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A tax invoice must be issued within 30 days of the transaction, detailing the freight charge, GST rate, and the GSTIN of both parties. Input tax credit can be claimed only if the consignor supplies a valid tax invoice.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<ul>
<li><strong>Transit Marine Insurance</strong>: For bike transport, the insurer typically calculates premiums as a percentage of the declared value. The standard band is 1.5% to 3% of the declared value, depending on the chosen coverage level and risk profile. A higher declared value increases the premium but also raises the maximum recoverable amount in case of loss.</li>
<li><strong>Premium Calculation Example</strong>: If the declared value of the bike is ₹30,000 and the carrier opts for 2% coverage, the annual premium would be ₹600 (₹30,000 × 0.02). The carrier can negotiate multi‑year discounts or bundled coverage with other cargo types.</li>
</ul></div>
